{
  "core_question": "What analyses must a nonprofit community hospital board conduct across clinical, legal, and financial dimensions when converting to for-profit via sale‑leaseback and spinning out a charitable foundation holding proceeds?",
  "rationale": "The transaction involves clinical service continuity, complex tax‑exempt status issues, and detailed financial structuring, requiring expertise from healthcare, legal, and finance specialists.",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "What are the key clinical and operational considerations a nonprofit community hospital board should evaluate when transitioning to a for‑profit model under a sale‑leaseback arrangement, including impacts on patient care quality, community benefit obligations, accreditation, and Medicare/Medicaid reimbursement eligibility?",
    "legal": "What are the primary legal issues a nonprofit hospital board must address when converting to a for‑profit entity, spinning out a charitable foundation that holds transaction proceeds, and executing a sale‑leaseback of its real estate, focusing on IRS tax‑exempt status preservation, state hospital conversion statutes, fiduciary duties, and lease terms?",
    "finance": "What financial analyses should the board conduct to evaluate the viability of converting a 90‑bed nonprofit hospital to for‑profit via sale‑leaseback, including valuation of assets and operations, projected cash flows, financing costs, tax consequences, and impact on the charitable foundation’s ability to fund community programs?"
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "IRS rules on sale‑leaseback and charitable foundation holding proceeds; state hospital conversion statutes; recent CMS reimbursement changes; private equity sponsor regulatory guidance."
}
